# Environment Variables for Production Deployment

## Required Variables

### VITE_API_URL
**Description**: Backend API endpoint
**Example**: `https://api.your-domain.com`
**Required**: Yes
**Note**: Must use HTTPS in production. Do not use localhost.

### VITE_ENVIRONMENT
**Description**: Deployment environment
**Options**: `development`, `staging`, `production`
**Required**: Yes
**Default**: `development`

## Optional Variables

### VITE_WS_URL
**Description**: WebSocket server endpoint
**Example**: `wss://api.your-domain.com`
**Default**: `ws://localhost:8000`

### VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS
**Description**: Enable analytics tracking
**Options**: `true`, `false`
**Default**: `false`

### VITE_SENTRY_DSN
**Description**: Sentry error tracking DSN
**Example**: `https://abc123@o123.ingest.sentry.io/456`
**Required**: No (recommended for production)

### VITE_CDN_URL
**Description**: CDN URL for static assets
**Example**: `https://cdn.your-domain.com`
**Required**: No (recommended for production performance)

## Vercel Configuration

Set these in Vercel Dashboard → Project Settings → Environment Variables

### Production Example:
```
VITE_API_URL=https://api.zenith-platform.com
VITE_ENVIRONMENT=production
VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true
VITE_WS_URL=wss://api.zenith-platform.com
```

### Development/Preview:
```
VITE_API_URL=/api/v1
VITE_ENVIRONMENT=development
VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=false
```

## Notes
- The application now uses **non-fatal validation** and will fall back to defaults if variables are missing
- You will see console warnings if required variables are not configured
- For strict validation during development, set `VITE_STRICT_ENV_CHECK=true`
